{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new functions and refactors existing ones to improve usability and compatibility. It also updates internal warnings and removes legacy Python 2 support, ensuring the library remains modern and robust.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The public API must expose a function named 'apply' that accepts an iterable of arguments and applies them to a given function. Additionally, 'identity' and 'thread_first' must be available as standard utility functions for data transformation pipelines."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The release must provide 'compose_left' and 'pipe' functions that allow for left-to-right composition and piping of data through a sequence of functions. These should behave consistently with existing composition utilities like 'compose'."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "A new function named 'peekn' must be exposed, which allows inspecting the first n items of an iterator without consuming them. The existing 'peek' function should remain available for inspecting a single item."
    },
    {
      "id": "m07",
      "text": "The 'fold' function must continue to support parallel execution across multiple processes, maintaining its previous interface for combining elements from an iterable using a specified function."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "Ensure that any breakpoint-related signatures or debugging hooks are correctly handled within the library's internal mechanisms, preserving expected behavior during interactive debugging sessions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14",
      "text": "The 'merge' and 'merge_with' functions must accept any Mapping type, not just dictionaries, allowing for broader compatibility with other mapping-like objects in the Python ecosystem."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "All listed functions including 'curry', 'Compose', 'excepts', and others must operate exclusively on Python 3 environments, removing any conditional logic or syntax specific to Python 2. The 'curried' alias must be available if referenced via 'functoolz'."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31",
      "text": "Warning messages generated by the library, particularly those related to configuration retrieval via 'get_config_from_root', must be clearer and more informative to aid users in diagnosing issues."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names are exported correctly and that the removal of Python 2 support does not break existing user code relying on Python 3 features. Verify that the new functions integrate seamlessly with the existing toolz ecosystem."
}
